.TH ZERODDS-WEBDDS-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-webdds-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-webdds-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/webdds-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the DDS-WEB gateway daemon binds HTTP,
which topic types it can resolve, and who may reach which Application.
The parser that reads it is
.IR crates/webdds-bridge/src/daemon/config.rs::DaemonConfig::from_config .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR listen ", " domain ", " log_level ", " max_body_bytes ", " tls ", "
.BR auth ", " metrics ", " acl ", " types ", " interfaces .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr and starts with the
defaults \(em watch the WARN log. A key inside a known section the
schema does not name, or a value of the wrong type, stops the start
with the file and line.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B listen
HTTP bind address, serving the REST PSM
.RI ( /dds/rest1 ),
the SOAP PSM
.RI ( /soap ),
and the WSDL description of both
.RI ( /wsdl )
on the one port. Default
.IR 127.0.0.1:8080 .
.TP
.B domain
Integer. The DDS domain a
.I domain_participant
resource is created on names its own
.I domain_id
in the request body \(em this key has no effect on that. It is the
domain the daemon's DDS-RPC client
.I DomainParticipant
is created on, when
.B interfaces
names at least one IDL file with an operation dispatched over SOAP
(see
.B interfaces
below); with no
.B interfaces
configured, no such participant is created and this key has no
effect at all. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.TP
.B max_body_bytes
DoS cap on a request's
.B Content-Length
or total chunked body size, in bytes. Default
.IR 8388608 " (8 MiB)."
.SS tls
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. With
.IR true ,
.B cert_file
and
.B key_file
are mandatory; the daemon refuses to start without them.
.TP
.B cert_file
Server certificate, PEM.
.TP
.B key_file
Server key, PEM.
.TP
.B client_ca_file
Trust anchor for mTLS client certificates
.RI ( "auth.mode: mtls" " needs this too)."
.SS auth
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " bearer " | " jwt " | " mtls .
.TP
.B bearer_token
Shared token accepted when
.B mode
is
.IR bearer .
.TP
.B bearer_subject
Subject that single token authenticates as. Default
.IR anonymous .
.TP
.B jwt
Sub-map for
.BR jwt :
.B public_key
(PEM file, PKCS#1 or SubjectPublicKeyInfo, RS256),
.BR issuer ,
.BR audience ,
.B required_claim
.RI ( claim=value ).
Without
.B public_key
the daemon does not start (exit 1).
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Toggles the Prometheus
.I /metrics
endpoint (a separate listener from
.BR listen ).
.TP
.B listen
Bind address for
.IR /metrics .
Default
.IR 127.0.0.1:9095 " if " enabled
and unset.
.SS acl
Map of
.IR "<application name>: { read: [...], write: [...] }" .
The resource unit is the
.B Application
name a request's path names, not the DDS topic underneath it \(em the
.B zerodds-bridge-security
ACL is topic-shaped, but a
.IR domain_participant / publisher / subscriber
operation names no topic at all, and the WebDDS object model's own
access-control model (OMG DDS-WEB 1.0 \(sc7.3) is scoped through the
object tree rooted at
.IR Application .
The subject is the one
.B auth.mode
yields:
.I anonymous
for
.BR none ,
the token's subject for
.BR bearer " and " jwt ,
the certificate identity for
.BR mtls .
An
.B unlisted
application default-denies once
.B auth.mode
is anything other than
.IR none .
.RS
.TP
.B read
Subjects allowed a
.BR GET / HEAD
on that application's subtree.
.TP
.B write
Subjects allowed a
.BR POST / PUT / DELETE .
.RE
.SS types
List of
.IR "{ name: <scoped type name>, idl_file: <path> }" " or "
.IR "{ name: <scoped type name>, xml_file: <path> }" .
Every entry names a type this gateway can resolve for a topic
(\fBPOST .../topics\fR's
.B type_name
field), from a config-named
.I .idl
file or a DDS-XML 1.0
.I <types>
document — exactly one of
.B idl_file
/
.B xml_file
per entry. A type not listed here must already be resolvable via
TypeLookup discovery
(\fIcrate::types_registry::TypeRegistry::resolve_discovered\fR) before
a topic names it.
.SS interfaces
List of
.I .idl
file paths whose
.I interface
declarations are described \(em name, and each operation's request/
reply type names \(em in the WSDL served at
.IR /wsdl ,
and dispatchable over SOAP: invoking one of these operations sends a
real DDS-RPC 1.0 request and waits for its reply, on the daemon's own
DDS-RPC client
.I DomainParticipant
(see
.B domain
above). Every named
.I interface
shares
.B one
request/reply topic pair (DDS-RPC 1.0 \(sc7.4.3/\(sc7.5.1.1, keyed by
operation), the same convention a
.I zerodds-idlc generate --lang rust/cpp
binding for the same
.I interface
follows \(em this daemon interoperates with such a generated
Requester/Replier, not only with itself. An operation naming no
configured
.I interface
(and no WebDDS object-model operation either) answers with a named
SOAP fault, never a silent no-op; a declared
.B raises
exception answers with a named fault too, not an empty or wrong
success.
.SH EXAMPLE
See
.I /etc/zerodds/webdds-bridged.yaml.example
(installed alongside this daemon).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-webdds-bridged (1).
